






@(1 = 1-2) Say to @wPN{Aradŋu}: this is what @wRN{Šulgi}, your lord, says:

@(3 = 3-5) The man to whom I have sent you is not your subordinate -- he will not  @varh[t3102.v1]{accept } @vart[t3102.v2,t3102.v1]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} change } orders from your hand! How can you ignore what he himself has done too, and that it is indeed so?

#etcsl#altGrpo
#etcsl#alt t3102.v1 t3102.v2
#etcsl#altGrpc

@(6 = 6-15) As I myself ordered, you were to secure the provinces, and to correctly guide the people and  @varh[t3102.v3]{make them obedient } @vart[t3102.v4,t3102.v3]{@varn{2 mss. have instead:} secure the foundations of the provinces }. When you approach the cities of the provinces, inform yourself precisely of their intentions, and inform yourself of the words of their dignitaries. Let my roar  @varh[t3102.v5]{be emitted over all the lands } @vart[t3102.v6,t3102.v5]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} fill all the lands } @vart[t3102.v7,t3102.v5]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} cover all the lands }. Let my powerful arm, my heroic arm, fall upon all the lands. Let my storm  @varh[t3102.v8]{cover } @vart[t3102.v9,t3102.v8]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} be released over } the Land. Make the …… disappear into the desert, and the robbers into the fields! Until you reach @wPN{Apillaša}, my 'Sage of the Assembly', ……! Let …….

#etcsl#altGrpo
#etcsl#alt t3102.v3 t3102.v4
#etcsl#alt t3102.v5 t3102.v6 t3102.v7
#etcsl#alt t3102.v8 t3102.v9
#etcsl#altGrpc

@(16 = 16-17) That was how I had instructed you. Why have you not acted as I ordered you?

@(18 = 18-26) If I do not make my 'Sage of the Assembly' feel just as important as I am, if he does not sit on a throne on a dais, furnished with a high-quality cloth cover (?), if his feet do not rest on a golden footstool, if he is not allowed by his own highest authority both to appoint and then to remove a governor from his function as governor, an official  @varh[t3102.v10]{from his charge } @vart[t3102.v11,t3102.v10]{@varn{some mss. have instead:} from his function as official } @vart[t3102.v12,t3102.v10]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} from an official }, if he does not kill or blind anyone, if he does not elevate his favourite over others -- how else can he secure the provinces?

#etcsl#altGrpo
#etcsl#alt t3102.v10 t3102.v11
#etcsl#alt t3102.v10 t3102.v11 t3102.v12
#etcsl#altGrpc

@(27 = 27-28) If you truly love me, you will not bear him a grudge!

@(29 = 29-30) You are important,  @varh[t3102.v13]{but you do not even know your own soldiers } @vart[t3102.v14,t3102.v13]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} and you even know the soldiers that are at @wPN{Apillaša's} disposal }. Your eyes have learnt something about  @varh[t3102.v15]{these men } @vart[t3102.v16,t3102.v15]{@varn{some mss. have instead:} @wPN{Apillaša's} men }, and about  @varh[t3102.v17]{@wPN{Apillaša's} heroism } @vart[t3102.v18,t3102.v17]{@varn{some mss. have instead:} my heroism }.

#etcsl#altGrpo
#etcsl#alt t3102.v13 t3102.v14
#etcsl#alt t3102.v15 t3102.v16
#etcsl#alt t3102.v17 t3102.v18
#etcsl#altGrpc

@(31 = 31-35) If  @varh[t3102.v19]{you, @wPN{Aradŋu}, are indeed my servant } @vart[t3102.v20,t3102.v19]{@varn{some mss. have instead:} you, @wPN{Aradŋu} and @wPN{Apillaša}, are indeed my servants }, you should both pay attention (?) to my written communications. Come to an understanding, you two! Secure the foundations of the provinces! It is urgent!

#etcsl#altGrpo
#etcsl#alt t3102.v19 t3102.v20
